    "body": "The shared literal fit repaired first sums but changed working computed-result choices and emitted numbers where Rust needed identifiers. This adds an artifact-bound literal routing component while preserving every inherited field of the accepted af337c28 model. Structural eligibility chooses the literal component only when no derived records remain; its learned Copy/Add/NoOperation choice decides whether numeric execution is appropriate. Original word-copy construction cases provide NoOperation supervision with numeric distractors.\n\nRetain c29ab982 at bounded literal-admission scope:\n- New complete conversations:12/16 parent →16/16; new literal answers8/16 →12/16; new identifier answers remain8/8.\n- Exposed prior independent-result set:12/16 →16/16, with no previously correct case lost.\n- Restores62/62 earlier responses and24/24 transfer; preserves48/48 dependent,28/28 exposed-name,28/28 long-context,5/5 persistent,6/6 numeric, three12-case prior role sets and58/58 computed construction trajectories.\n- Eight generated identifier-return functions execute24 semantic assertions. The real CLI returns the requested identifier rather than a distractor number.\n\nThe matched literal exact-code control gets the same new-transfer scores; no additional angular-distance advantage is established. Four new abstention texts still fail. Construction is103/103 routing targets but95/103 full responses. General language, algorithm synthesis, mixed arithmetic-to-prose conversation and frontier capability remain unqualified. The next change is supported-word versus abstention answer routing after NoOperation, preserving this admission behavior.\n\nValidation: rebuilt probe/CLI, seven focused typed tests, kernel source check, actual three-turn zero-allocation and checkpoint checks, full parent-field equality and artifact-mutation rejection, generated Rust execution, formatting, native policy, claim wording and diff checks pass. Broad dormant release QA is NOT_RUN. Serving adds no matmul, float projection, dense transformer or provider/LLM correction.\n\n246.540s monitored model work and359.332s engineering. Cumulative model use3168.126/3210s; all prior charges retained. Pre-recorded+240s cumulative extension; no storage allowance increase, deletions or external model compute. This builds on merged #1157 (a52575dd); measured source identities match after rebase. Protected hosted checks are pending, and compatibility acknowledgements are not model-quality evidence.\n\nAdvances #1139 and #1140 without closing their broader criteria. Details and artifact/report identities: `docs/native_geometric_literal_admission_1139.md` and its compact evidence record.\n",
